{"raw": {"https://workforcenow.cloud.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=71919c4b-9ac0-4e36-8f03-d1e5235783c0&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=58469349_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Academic Coach", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-10\n\nLocation: Livonia\n\nTRIO Academic Coach", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.cloud.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=71919c4b-9ac0-4e36-8f03-d1e5235783c0&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=38957433_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Student Worker", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-12\n\nLocation: Livonia\n\nStudent Worker\u00a0 Position Type: \u00a0Student Assistant (Part-Time) Department Assignment: \u00a0Various Academic Departments and Athletics\u00a0 Location: \u00a0Madonna University \u2013 Livonia, Michigan About Madonna University Madonna University is one of the nation\u2019s largest Franciscan universities, serving approximately 2,000 undergraduate and graduate students. Rooted in Catholic and Franciscan traditions, the University emphasizes intellectual rigor, professional preparation, ethical leadership, and service to others. Madonna University\u2019s community is committed to learning that leads to meaningful service and a positive impact on society. With alumni on every continent except Antarctica, graduates apply their knowledge and skills across diverse professions while improving the lives of others. Essential Responsibilities Responsibilities vary by assignment and may include: Assist faculty and staff with academic and administrative projects. Support classroom preparation and instructional activities. Assist with research, data collection, and departmental projects. Provide assistance with tutoring, learning support, laboratories, or academic resource centers, when applicable. Assist with organizing files, reports, records, and departmental documentation. Support student engagement activities and departmental events. Provide excellent customer service to students, faculty, staff, and visitors. Perform other duties that support the mission and operations of the assigned department. Position Summary Madonna University invites applications from undergraduate students seeking valuable work experience while pursuing their degree. Student Assistants in academic departments support faculty, staff, and students through academic services, research assistance, departmental projects, and other activities that contribute to the University\u2019s educational mission. These positions provide students with opportunities to develop professional skills while gaining practical experience in an academic environment. Assignments are available in various academic departments and support units based on departmental needs and the student\u2019s qualifications, interests, skills, and availability. Essential Responsibilities Responsibilities vary by assignment and may include: Assist faculty and academic staff with departmental projects and initiatives. Support classroom preparation, laboratory activities, and academic resources. Assist with research activities, data collection, and organization of project materials under faculty or staff supervision. Help prepare instructional materials, reports, presentations, and departmental documentation. Support tutoring, peer mentoring, student success initiatives, or academic support services, when applicable. Assist with academic events, workshops, meetings, and student engagement activities. Organize records, maintain information, and provide general support to academic departments. Provide professional and courteous assistance to students, faculty, staff, and visitors. Perform other duties that support the mission and operations of the assigned department. Minimum Qualifications Applicants must: Be enrolled as an undergraduate student at Madonna University. Maintain satisfactory academic progress. Demonstrate strong communication, organizational, and interpersonal skills. Be dependable, professional, and able to work independently and collaboratively. Maintain confidentiality when handling sensitive information. Possess basic computer skills, including Microsoft Office, and be willing to learn University software and systems. Compensation and Benefits Hourly wage in accordance with University student employment guidelines. Approximately 10\u201315 hours per week, based on departmental needs and student availability. Flexible scheduling that supports academic success. Opportunities to develop communication, organizational, research, technology, and professional skills. Department Assignment Student Assistants may be assigned to academic schools, departments, laboratories, libraries, research projects, tutoring and learning centers, or other academic support units. Assignments are based on departmental needs and the student\u2019s qualifications, experience, interests, and availability. Specific responsibilities, work schedules, and reporting relationships will be provided at the time of appointment. Madonna University is committed to providing a welcoming, inclusive, and student-centered learning community. We encourage qualified students from all backgrounds to apply.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.cloud.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=71919c4b-9ac0-4e36-8f03-d1e5235783c0&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=26657918_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Associate Registrar", "description": "Posted: 2026-07-20\n\nLocation: Livonia\n\nAssociate Registrar Department: Office of the Registrar Reports To: Assistant Vice President of Enrollment Services and Registrar \u00a0 Level: 8 SUMMARY The Associate Registrar serves as an advisor to the Assistant Vice President and Registrar and provides operational leadership for the daily activities of the Enrollment Center. This position coordinates academic records, registration services, and office operations while supporting university policies and procedures. The Associate Registrar resolves complex student record issues and collaborates with campus partners to ensure accurate, efficient, and student-centered services. ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Assists the AVP of Enrollment Services and Registrar in the administration and daily operation of the Enrollment Center, providing operational leadership and serving on behalf of the Registrar as delegated. Provides operational leadership for the Enrollment Center by coordinating daily workflow, front-line services, staffing, scheduling, and customer service to ensure efficient delivery of Enrollment Services. Coordinates academic records administration and registration services to ensure the accuracy, integrity, and timely maintenance of student academic records and enrollment activity. Coordinates specialized registration and academic record processes, including consortium registrations, dual enrollment, course overloads, graduate professional development, applied music, academic standing actions, grade processing, and related record transactions. Researches and resolves complex registration, enrollment, grading, and student record issues while collaborating with faculty, academic departments, and campus partners to ensure appropriate resolution. Coordinates front-line student account support and cashiering functions, including account review, journal entries, miscellaneous group entries, receipt of payments, and related Enrollment Center financial transactions in collaboration with Student Financial Services. Prepares, reviews, and distributes operational reports; monitors data integrity; identifies discrepancies; and coordinates corrective actions as appropriate. Develops, maintains, and coordinates departmental procedures, technical documentation, and training resources to support consistent operations and cross-functional knowledge throughout Enrollment Services. Supervises Enrollment Center staff, temporary employees, and student employees by assigning work, monitoring daily operations, providing training and coaching, and supporting high-quality customer service. Collaborates with academic and administrative departments to coordinate student enrollment, attendance, registration, academic records, and related operational processes. Represents the Office of the Registrar on University committees, consortium activities, and institutional initiatives as assigned. Other duties as assigned. SUPERVISORY RESPONSIBILITIES Carries out supervisory responsibilities in accordance with the organization\u2019s policies and applicable laws. Responsibilities may include interviewing, hiring and training; planning, assigning and directing work of student workers; addressing complaints and resolving problems. \u00a0 QUALIFICATIONS The above statements reflect the general responsibilities of the position and should not be construed as a detailed description of all the work requirements that may be inherent in this position.\u00a0 To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily. The requirements listed below are representative of the knowledge, skill, and/or ability required. \u00a0 EDUCATION AND EXPERIENCE Bachelor\u2019s degree from a four-year college or university; and two to three years related experience and/or training or equivalent combination of education and experience. Working knowledge of Microsoft Office. \u00a0 MANAGERIAL SKILLS Essential managerial skills include directing (organizing, energizing, and supervising), negotiating, planning and problem solving, facilitating the work of others, clarifying goals and objectives, obtaining and giving feedback, delegating, team building, effectively communicating, evaluating, and initiating change. Ability to define problems, collect data, establish facts, and draw valid conclusions in an extensive variety of situations. \u00a0 LANGUAGE SKILLS Ability to read, analyze, and interpret general business periodicals, professional journals, technical procedures, or governmental regulations. Ability to effectively present information and respond to questions from groups of managers, customers, and the general public. \u00a0 MATHEMATICAL SKILLS \u00a0 Ability to add, subtract, multiply and divide in all units of measure, use whole numbers, fractions and decimals. Ability to compute rate, ratio and percent and to draw and interpret bar graphs. REASONING ABILITY Ability to solve practical problems and deal with a variety of concrete variables in situations where only limited standardization exists. Ability to interpret a variety of instructions furnished in written, oral, diagram or schedule form. \u00a0 PHYSICAL DEMANDS The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. While performing the duties of this job, the employee is regularly required to stand; walk; sit; use hands to finger, handle, or feel; and talk or hear. The employee is occasionally required to climb or balance; and stoop, kneel, crouch or crawl. The employee must occasionally lift and/or move up to 25 pounds. \u00a0 WORK ENVIRONMENT The work environment characteristics described here are representative of those an employee encounters while performing the essential functions of this job.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.cloud.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=71919c4b-9ac0-4e36-8f03-d1e5235783c0&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=24335448_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Adjunct Clinical Instructor (Undergraduate Program)", "description": "Posted: 2026-07-15\n\nLocation: Livonia\n\nAdjunct Clinical Instructor (Undergraduate Program)\u00a0 Madonna University is a Franciscan, Catholic co-educational liberal arts university located in Livonia, Michigan. \u00a0The growing student body of 4,400 is an exciting and diverse mix of traditional and non traditional commuter students. \u00a0At Madonna University, teaching is of primary importance, and faculty members actively participate in University governance and academic affairs. The Nursing department of the College of Nursing and Health offers Bachelors, Masters, and Doctor of Nursing Practice degrees, and post-graduate certificates. \u00a0The undergraduate program includes pre-licensure and degree completion students. \u00a0The graduate program offers a number of specialized options for advanced practice nursing roles and nursing administration roles, and a Doctor of Nursing Practice degree focused on leadership within Aggregate/Systems/Organizations RESPONSIBILITIES Compliance with all ACE-MAPP requirements, supervise students in the application of nursing theory to the clinical setting. \u00a0Conduct pre-clinical conferences to determine student level preparedness, ensuring safety, effective clinical experience, review care maps/worksheets and other assignments. \u00a0 Grades all written assignments, observes and records students\u2019 clinical behaviors. \u00a0Be familiar with the clinical agency\u2019s procedures by attending orientation sessions prior to the start of a course if needed. \u00a0Attend online or departmental course meetings on an as needed basis.\u00a0 QUALIFICATIONS\u00a0 1. Master\u2019s or higher degree in Nursing preferred, BSN required 2. Licensed as registered nurse in Michigan or eligible for same 3. Strong interpersonal relationship and organizational skills required The successful candidate will articulate a commitment to the University\u2019s mission and goals, the values of the nursing profession, diversity and social justice, and will offer a vision for the nursing curriculum reflecting the needs of persons in today\u2019s society. Madonna University is a Catholic institution founded by the Felician Sisters, and guided by the values of St. Francis. Candidates must be committed to excellence in teaching, scholarship, and service, and support the Mission of the University. We are an equal opportunity employer committed to a culturally diverse workforce. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the United States. Verification of employment eligibility will be required at the time of hire. Thank you for your interest in employment opportunities at Madonna University.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.cloud.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=71919c4b-9ac0-4e36-8f03-d1e5235783c0&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=24063512_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Head Athletic Trainer", "description": "Posted: 2026-07-15\n\nLocation: Livonia\n\nSUMMARY Athletics Athletic Director September 2023 The position is responsible for all aspects of the Madonna University health care for intercollegiate student-athletes in conjunction with all athletic training staff. Establishes and maintains lines of communications with team physician and other athletic trainers. ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES\u00a0 1. Oversees the overall management of the training room operations to include ordering supplies and maintaining inventory, upkeep and cleanliness and proper working order of the athletic training facilities and equipment on a daily basis, providing adequate coverage of the facility and working with staff to ensure coverage of all athletic events. \u00a02. Oversees athletic trainers to help manage and assist the team physician in the pre-participation of physical exams for each student-athlete.\u00a0 3. Maintains medical records for all student-athletes to include physical exams, insurance and family information, medical histories, records of injury evaluation, records of daily treatment and records of each insurance claim filed. \u00a0 Assists with coordinating insurance claim processing with athletic business manager and Athletic Director.\u00a0 4. Implements injury prevention programs whose minimum requirements include pre-game and practice taping and strapping, implementing flexibility and strengthening programs, consulting coaches on environmental considerations (heat and humidity) and maintaining and applying protective equipment.\u00a0 5. Evaluates athletic injuries to include obtaining medical history and running a battery testing procedures to identify the injury and judge the severity of the injury as directed by standardized protocols.\u00a0 6. Treats injuries by providing emergency care and first aid procedures for the injured student-athletes as directed by standardized procedures and/or a physician\u2019s recommendation.\u00a0 7. Establishes the proper referral procedure for injuries which require the opinion of the team physician or medical specialist, emergency room, orthopedist, internist, dentist, etc.\u00a0 8. Designs and supervises implementation and rehabilitation programs for each injury which at a minimum includes implementation of proper rehabilitation protocol as determined by established medical standards or a physician\u2019s prescription, monitoring and documenting the individuals\u2019 progress while adjusting the program the student-athletes tolerance and establishing a safe and graduated return to activity or the sport.\u00a0 9. Maintains NATA certification by following standards of continuing education.\u00a0 10. Travels with teams to designated events, primarily post-season championships.\u00a0 11. Provides practices and home game coverage for designed sports which may include weekend coverage.\u00a0 12. Assists with student employment processes as needed.\u00a0 13. Represents the athletic training room on the athletic department leadership council. \u00a0\u00a0 14. Other duties as assigned. SUPERVISORY RESPONSIBILITIES\u00a0 Carries out supervisory responsibilities in accordance with the organization\u2019s policies and applicable laws. Responsibilities may include interviewing, hiring and training; planning, assigning and directing work of employees AND/OR student workers; addressing complaints and resolving problems. MADONNA UNIVERSITY RESERVES THE RIGHT TO ASSIGN OR REASSIGN DUTIES AND \u00a0 ESPONSIBILITIES TO THIS JOB AT ANY TIME QUALIFICATIONS \u00a0 The above statements reflect the general responsibilities of the position and should not be construed as a detailed description of all the work requirements that may be inherent in this position. To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily. The requirements listed below are representative of the knowledge, skill, and/or ability required. Must have a valid driver\u2019s license, commercially insurable driving record, and own transportation. May be required to work outside of normal working hours. Travel may be required, evening and weekend hours expected. EDUCATION AND EXPERIENCE \u00a0 Head Athletic Trainer Page 2 Bachelor\u2019s degree; master\u2019s degree preferred; CSCS Certification preferred, or three to five years related experience and training; or equivalent combination of education and experience and training. \u00a0 May be required to work outside normal business hours. MANAGERIAL SKILLS Essential managerial skills include directing (organizing, energizing, and supervising), negotiating, planning and problem solving, facilitating the work of others, clarifying goals and objectives, obtaining and giving feedback, delegating, team building, effectively communicating, evaluating, and initiating change. Ability to define problems, collect data, establish facts, and draw valid conclusions in an extensive variety of situations. Ability to appropriately handle confidential material and maintain integrity and confidentiality of data. RELATIONAL SKILLS Embrace, uphold, and promote the values of Madonna University, with a sense of commitment to our mission and the future of the institution. \u00a0Commitment to diversity, equity, inclusion, and cultural awareness in order to strengthen a sense of belonging for all students. \u00a0Ability to demonstrate genuine empathy and care for students, their challenges, and their success. \u00a0Ability to work collaboratively and enthusiastically in a team environment. \u00a0Demonstrated knowledge of and sensitivity to students from diverse backgrounds and the ability to recognize ad respond to the unique needs of diverse, underrepresented, and marginalized students. \u00a0\u00a0 LANGUAGE SKILLS Ability to read, analyze, and interpret general business periodicals, professional journals, technical procedures, or governmental regulations. Ability to effectively present information and respond to questions from groups of managers, customers, and the general public. MATHEMATICAL SKILLS \u00a0 Ability to add, subtract, multiply and divide in all units of measure, use whole numbers, fractions and decimals. \u00a0Ability to compute rate, ratio and percent and to draw and interpret bar graphs.\u00a0 REASONING ABILITY Ability to solve practical problems and deal with a variety of concrete variables in situations where only limited standardization exists. Ability to interpret a variety of instructions furnished in written, oral, diagram or schedule form.\u00a0 PHYSICAL DEMANDS The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. While performing the duties of this job, the employee is regularly required to stand; walk; use hands to touch, handle, or feel; and talk or hear. The employee is may be required to reach with hands or arms, stoop, kneel, or crouch. Employee may occasionally lift and/or move up to 15 pounds. Reasonable accommodations may be considered to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions.\u00a0 WORK ENVIRONMENT\u00a0 The work environment characteristics described here are representative of those an employee encounters while performing the essential functions of this job.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.cloud.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=71919c4b-9ac0-4e36-8f03-d1e5235783c0&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=22992714_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Assistant Coach PT", "description": "Posted: 2026-07-08\n\nLocation: Livonia\n\nSUMMARY\u00a0 Assist head coach in all assigned duties including, but not limited to, recruiting, coaching, practice planning, and academic support. ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES\u00a0 1. Attends and assists in running practices.\u00a0 2. Scouts other teams electronically and on site.\u00a0 3. Develops and implements practice plans.\u00a0 4. Works individually with players on skill development.\u00a0 5. Assists with fundraising.\u00a0 6. Attends high school and showcase events for recruiting.\u00a0 7. Assists in conducting summer camps, clinics, and other community service activities.\u00a0 8. Other duties as assigned. QUALIFICATIONS\u00a0 The above statements reflect the general responsibilities of the position and should not be construed as a detailed description of all the work requirements that may be inherent in this position. To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily. The requirements listed below are representative of the knowledge, skill, and/or ability required. EDUCATION AND EXPERIENCE\u00a0 High school diploma or general education degree (GED); one to three years coaching experience required (preferably at the collegiate level) in the specific sport to be coached and/or equivalent combination of education and experience. Prior college level playing experience and work with sport clinics and camps a plus.\u00a0 This job requires the individual to work nights and weekends with expectation of potentially extensive travel.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.cloud.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=71919c4b-9ac0-4e36-8f03-d1e5235783c0&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=20821413_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Athletic Trainer", "description": "Posted: 2026-07-08\n\nLocation: Livonia\n\nSUMMARY This position will help manage the overall health care of Madonna University intercollegiate student athletes in conjunction with all athletic training staff. Maintains lines of communication with team physicians, coaches and other athletic trainers. Sport assignments will be determined by the Head Athletic Trainer. ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES \u00a01. Manages training room operations to include maintaining inventory, upkeep and cleanliness and proper working order of the athletic training facilities and equipment on a daily basis, providing adequate coverage of the facility and working with athletic staff to ensure coverage of all athletic events.\u00a0 2. Maintains medical records for all student athletes to include physical exam forms, insurance and family information,medical histories, records of each injury evaluation, records of daily treatment and records of each insurance claim filed. Assists Head Athletic Trainer and Business Office with coordinating insurance claims processing.\u00a0 3. Implements injury prevention programs whose minimum requirements include pre-game and practice taping and strapping, implementing flexibility and strengthening programs, consulting coaches on environmental considerations(cold, heat andhumidity) andmaintaining and applying protective equipment.\u00a0 4. Evaluates athletic injuries to include obtaining medical history and running a battery of testing procedures to identify the injury and judge the severity of the injury as directed by standardized protocols.\u00a0 5. Treats injuries by providing emergency care and first aid procedures for the injured athletes as directed by standardized procedures and/or a physician's recommendation.\u00a0 6. Establishes the proper referral procedure for injuries which require the opinion of the team physician or medical specialist, emergency room, orthopedist, internist, dentist, etc.\u00a0 7. Designs and supervises implementation of rehabilitation programs for each injury which at a minimum includes implementation of proper rehabilitation protocol as determined by established medical standards or a physician\u2019s prescription, monitoring and documenting the individuals' progress while adjusting the program to the athlete's tolerance and establishing a safe and graduated return to activity or the sport.\u00a0 8. Provides practice and home game coverage for designated sports which may include weekend coverage.\u00a0 9. Maintains NATA certification by following standards of continuing education.\u00a0 10. Assists with student employment processes as needed.\u00a0 11. Other duties as assigned.\u00a0 SUPERVISORY RESPONSIBILITIES\u00a0 Carries out supervisory responsibilities in accordance with the organization\u2019s policies and applicable laws. Responsibilities may include interviewing, hiring and training; planning, assigning and directing work of student workers; addressing complaints and resolving problems.", "department": ""}}, "rows": {"https://workforcenow.cloud.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=71919c4b-9ac0-4e36-8f03-d1e5235783c0&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=58469349_1&lang=en_US": {"school_id": 651, "posting_url": "https://workforcenow.cloud.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=71919c4b-9ac0-4e36-8f03-d1e5235783c0&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=58469349_1&lang=en_US", "job_title_in_post": "Academic Coach", "position_type": "Unclassified", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "", "deadline_of_application": "", "posted_date": "2026-09-10", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://workforcenow.cloud.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=71919c4b-9ac0-4e36-8f03-d1e5235783c0&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=38957433_1&lang=en_US": {"school_id": 651, "posting_url": "https://workforcenow.cloud.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=71919c4b-9ac0-4e36-8f03-d1e5235783c0&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=38957433_1&lang=en_US", "job_title_in_post": "Student Worker", "position_type": "Unclassified", "job_term": "Part-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "", "deadline_of_application": "", "posted_date": "2026-08-12", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://workforcenow.cloud.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=71919c4b-9ac0-4e36-8f03-d1e5235783c0&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=26657918_1&lang=en_US": {"school_id": 651, "posting_url": "https://workforcenow.cloud.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=71919c4b-9ac0-4e36-8f03-d1e5235783c0&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=26657918_1&lang=en_US", "job_title_in_post": "Associate Registrar", "position_type": "Unclassified", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "", "deadline_of_application": "", "posted_date": "2026-07-20", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://workforcenow.cloud.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=71919c4b-9ac0-4e36-8f03-d1e5235783c0&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=24335448_1&lang=en_US": {"school_id": 651, "posting_url": "https://workforcenow.cloud.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=71919c4b-9ac0-4e36-8f03-d1e5235783c0&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=24335448_1&lang=en_US", "job_title_in_post": "Adjunct Clinical Instructor (Undergraduate Program)", "position_type": "Lecturer", "job_term": "Part-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "", "deadline_of_application": "", "posted_date": "2026-07-15", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://workforcenow.cloud.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=71919c4b-9ac0-4e36-8f03-d1e5235783c0&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=24063512_1&lang=en_US": {"school_id": 651, "posting_url": "https://workforcenow.cloud.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=71919c4b-9ac0-4e36-8f03-d1e5235783c0&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=24063512_1&lang=en_US", "job_title_in_post": "Head Athletic Trainer", "position_type": "Unclassified", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "", "deadline_of_application": "", "posted_date": "2026-07-15", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://workforcenow.cloud.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=71919c4b-9ac0-4e36-8f03-d1e5235783c0&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=22992714_1&lang=en_US": {"school_id": 651, "posting_url": "https://workforcenow.cloud.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=71919c4b-9ac0-4e36-8f03-d1e5235783c0&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=22992714_1&lang=en_US", "job_title_in_post": "Assistant Coach PT", "position_type": "Unclassified", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "", "deadline_of_application": "", "posted_date": "2026-07-08", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://workforcenow.cloud.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=71919c4b-9ac0-4e36-8f03-d1e5235783c0&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=20821413_1&lang=en_US": {"school_id": 651, "posting_url": "https://workforcenow.cloud.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=71919c4b-9ac0-4e36-8f03-d1e5235783c0&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=20821413_1&lang=en_US", "job_title_in_post": "Athletic Trainer", "position_type": "Unclassified", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "", "deadline_of_application": "", "posted_date": "2026-07-08", "position_start_date": ""}}, "school_id": 651, "status": "complete", "updated_at": "2026-10-27T00:35:38+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-10-27T00:35:38+00:00", "last_error": ""}